translation:
Homage to Tāre, the swift and heroic;
To Tuttāre, she who dispels all fears;
To Ture, the liberatress who grants all benefits;
To the syllables of Svāhā, I bow to you.

You are the supreme essence churned from the ocean of the two accumulations;
By the mere arising of your moon-like form of marks and signs in the mind,
You grant the respite of longevity and primordial wisdom;
I prostrate to the Noble Lady, the Wish-Fulfilling Wheel.

Your heart-mind is the expanse of non-dual primordial wisdom;
Though you have withdrawn the engagement and emergence of conceptual elaborations,
You possess boundless splendor of awareness and love;
I prostrate to the Noble Lady, the Wish-Fulfilling Wheel.
